.1 at move 12)."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "D3 was the decisive error: 38.9 points lost, with Black's lead going from +33.0 to +71.9. It filled the empty point D3 in White's row of stones on row 3 and row 4, with Black on C2 and D1 below. The engine's first choice was B2."}, {"turn": 39, "text": "A6 by the 12k lost 35.0 points, cutting the lead from +72.0 to +37.0, and the engine preferred C1. It was the biggest swing the 12k's side produced, but Black still led by 37.0 and Opus 5.5 never got closer."}, {"turn": 50, "text": "G1 and the nearby edge moves (F1, H1) cost little each, and the endgame stayed around +36 to +38. Opus 5.5 played tidily here, but the lead was too large to recover, and it resigned after move 53."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran was libs.py, which parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties, plus cat/tail/append on the games.md log; none of it chooses, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}